00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
Now that you've written your sentence down, try shifting the stress around in

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:08,040
your own language by going through the stress patterns. Don't try to put on a

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:12,560
particular American or other accent. Just concentrate on stressing a different word

4
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:17,740
in the sentence each time you say it. For example, if your language is German, ich

5
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:21,820
habe nicht gesagt, dass er das Geld gestohlen hat, you would change the stress

6
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:25,000
to, ich habe nicht gesagt, dass er das Geld gestohlen

7
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:33,340
If you translated it into French, you would say,

8
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:36,680
Or,

9
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:44,460
In Japanese, many people think there are no intonation changes, but if you hear

10
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:50,140
someone say, you'll realize that it has similarities to every other language.

11
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:54,700
Or,

12
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:03,920
No matter how strange it may sound to you, stress each different word several times

13
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:08,520
in your language. You may notice that with some words it sounds perfectly normal, but

14
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:12,660
with other words it sounds very strange. Or you may find that in your language,

15
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:17,440
rather than stressing a word, you prefer to change the word order or substitute

16
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:22,220
another word. Whatever you do is fine, as long as you realize where your language

17
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,720
patterns are similar to and different from the American English intonation patterns.

18
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:33,160
Then, when you do it again in English, it'll be much easier. Note, an excellent

19
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:37,600
exercise is to practice speaking your native language with an American accent.

20
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:42,220
If you can sound like an American speaking your native language, imagine how easy it

21
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:46,620
would be to speak English with an American accent. Practice shifting the stressed

22
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:48,120
words in your native language.
